  "body": "## What changed\nThe Fanuc post (`assets/posts/fanuc.cps`) wrote a doubled sign whenever a probe's expected value was negative in the active work offset. This happened in two places:\n\n| Where | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `onProbeResult` deviation, edge at X -15 | `#190=#100--17` | `#190=#100+17` |\n| `onProbeResult`, corner at (-15, -10), Y | `#191=#104--12` | `#191=#104+12` |\n| `onProbeMove` no-contact check | `IF[ABS[#5061--12]LT0.001]...` | `IF[ABS[#5061+12]LT0.001]...` |\n| expected value 0 or -0 | `#190=#100-0` | `#190=#100` |\n\n- A new helper, `minusU(expr, v)`, writes `expr - v` with v's sign folded into the operator. A value that formats to 0 adds no term.\n- The output stays unbracketed: macro B's arithmetic form is `#i=#j-#k`. This keeps `probe_bore_centre.nc` byte-identical. The bracketed option and why it was dropped are in `docs/decisions/377-fanuc-probe-sign.md`.\n- The change stays clear of the comment block that #360 and #376 edit in fanuc.cps (lines 225-320).\n- Other posts:\n  - fanuc-lathe and heidenhain have no probe output.\n  - The Haas, Mazak, Sinumerik and Tormach probe hooks arrive with #360 and #376, which fix the same pattern on their own branches.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test fanuc_post`: 11/11 pass.\n- `--test probe_op`: 11/11 pass. No existing golden changed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (after merging upstream/main): every app suite passes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `edge_probe_at_negative_x_folds_the_sign`: new golden `fanuc/probe_edge_negative_x.nc`.\n- `corner_probe_at_negative_xy_folds_both_signs`: new golden `fanuc/probe_corner_negative.nc`.\n- `edge_probe_at_zero_writes_the_bare_mean`\n- Each probe test also asserts that no posted line contains `--`, `+-` or `-+`.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No real Fanuc control or macro-B simulator has run this. **It changes posted G-code, so it stays a draft until the maintainer does a Hub run or test cut.**\n\nChangelog: Fanuc probe post no longer writes a doubled sign (`#100--17`) for an edge or corner probe at a negative expected position (#377)\n\nFixes #377\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
